# Brewfile
#
# The Packages for each Machine, grouped by purpose. chezmoi places this file
# at ~/.Brewfile. One file serves macOS and Linux (see docs/adr/0002).
#
# How to use this file
# --------------------
# chezmoi runs `brew bundle --global` when this file or ~/.Brewfile.local
# changes. To run the commands yourself:
#
# Install everything listed here:
#     brew bundle --global
#
# Check what is missing, without installing anything:
#     brew bundle check --global --verbose
#
# List installed Packages that are NOT in this file (dry run, nothing removed):
#     brew bundle cleanup --global
#
# Remove those Packages. This also removes unlisted Go, npm, uv, krew and
# cargo packages, so read the dry-run output first:
#     brew bundle cleanup --global --force
#
# Adding a Package
# ----------------
# Put the line in the group it belongs to, with a one-line comment above it
# that describes the Package. Put casks and macOS-only formulae under
# `if OS.mac?`, Linux-only entries under `if OS.linux?` and winget entries
# under `if OS.wsl?`. Put Private Packages in ~/.Brewfile.local, which is not
# tracked (see docs/adr/0003).

